    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the speed-oriented ceiling of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (77.20), whose matchup against Bradley provides the day's premier opportunity. By leveraging a favorable platoon advantage (+14%) and the slow delivery of the opposing pitcher, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our top-tier target for stolen bases. **Yordan Alvarez** (68.98) remains a central figure despite the lefty-lefty disadvantage; his elite xwOBA (0.475) mitigates the platoon penalty, while **Colt Keith** (68.51) benefits significantly from a soft matchup against Rodriguez, showing high utility in the #3 spot. **Trea Turner** (67.03) and **Kyle Schwarber** (64.96) offer strong, stable production, providing the necessary volume at the top of the order to keep our Roto pace competitive.\n\nThe most difficult decision was the final utility slot, where **Junior Caminero** (65.10) narrowly edged out the bench depth of **Casey Schmitt** (48.22). While **Casey Schmitt** carries a decent floor, he failed to reach our operational mandate of 40 points, whereas **Junior Caminero** provides a superior park-adjusted ceiling (+7%) that outweighs the 39% rain risk at his venue. Our biggest risks today are centered on those weather concerns in **Caleb Durbin**\u2019s (55.24) and **Junior Caminero**'s games; if the rain holds off, both possess the profile to outperform their projections. We are carefully monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Dillon Dingler** and **Colt Keith**, but based on current trends, we are confident in their roles. **Carson Benge** (38.04) was considered but ultimately benched as he fell below our strict daily efficiency floor, leaving us to prioritize the high-upside starters across the board.",
